    "summary": "Mixed‑energy Syracuse '82 with a blazing Let It Grow & stellar PIB>UJB segue.",
    "review": "The April 8, 1982 show at the Onondaga County War Memorial swings between uneven and exhilarating. The first set never quite finds its footing – “Feel Like A Stranger” and “They Love Each Other” feel tentative, while “Let It Grow” erupts as a smoking highlight that showcases Jerry’s fierce commitment. The second set is where the night truly shines: a seamless Playing In The Band → Uncle John’s Band transition launches into an inspired Estimated Prophet and a soaring Eyes Of The World, capped by a wild PIB sandwich that carries the band all the way to a raucous Johnny B. Goode. Energy peaks high in the latter half, though some listeners note occasional sloppiness from Jerry later on. Overall, the concert is a mixed‑energy affair with enough fire and memorable moments to merit a spin, especially for fans of the early‑’80s era.",
